many 250px+ columns as fit, stretching to fill, with no media queries. This is the modern responsive grid pattern, replacing float\u002Fflexbox hacks.",[286,1363,1364,1357,1366,1368,1369,1371],{},[297,1365,1356],{},[38,1367,702],{}," for page-level layouts — it's a visual ASCII representation of the layout in CSS, self-documenting and easy to modify. Each named area must form a rectangle; use ",[38,1370,706],{}," for empty cells.",[286,1373,1374,1357,1376,1378,1379,1382,1383,1386,1387,1389,1390,1392,1393,706],{},[297,1375,1356],{},[38,1377,89],{}," for proportional track sizing — ",[38,1380,1381],{},"1fr 2fr"," gives a 1:2 ratio; ",[38,1384,1385],{},"200px 1fr"," gives a fixed sidebar + fluid content. ",[38,1388,89],{}," distributes ",[18,1391,205],{}," space (after fixed tracks), so it's the grid equivalent of flexbox's ",[38,1394,1395],{},"flex-grow",[286,1397,1398,1400],{},[297,1399,1356],{},": use Grid for two-dimensional layouts (rows + columns) and Flexbox for one-dimensional (a row or a column) — Grid is for \"a 2D grid of items\" (page layout, dashboards); Flexbox is for \"a row of items\" (navbars, button groups). Many layouts combine both (a grid of flex-card components).",[286,1402,1403,1405,1406,1409],{},[297,1404,1356],{},": use subgrid (2023+) when a nested grid should align with the parent's tracks — ",[38,1407,1408],{},"grid-template-columns: subgrid"," makes the item's grid use the parent's columns, so nested content aligns. Useful for forms, data tables, and aligned components.",[23,1411,1413],{"id":1412},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[283,1415,1416,1432,1448,1469,1477,1490,1502,1519,1527,1533],{},[286,1417,1418,62,1424,1426,1427,1429,1430,706],{},[297,1419,1420,279,1422],{},[38,1421,252],{},[38,1423,267],{},[38,1425,252],{}," keeps empty tracks (space goes to them); ",[38,1428,267],{}," collapses empty tracks (space goes to existing items, stretching them). For \"cards that stretch to fill the row,\" use ",[38,1431,267],{},[286,1433,1434,62,1441,1443,1444,1447],{},[297,1435,1436,1389,1438,1440],{},[38,1437,89],{},[18,1439,205],{}," space",[38,1442,209],{}," with a 200px item in the first column doesn't give equal columns — the first column gets at least 200px (its content min), then free space is split. Use ",[38,1445,1446],{},"minmax(0, 1fr)"," to allow shrinking below content.",[286,1449,1450,62,1457,1459,1460,1462,1463,1465,1466,1468],{},[297,1451,1452,279,1454],{},[38,1453,1446],{},[38,1455,1456],{},"1fr",[38,1458,1456],{}," has a minimum of ",[38,1461,107],{}," (content size); ",[38,1464,1446],{}," has a minimum of 0, allowing the track to shrink below content. Use ",[38,1467,1446],{}," when content might overflow.",[286,1470,1471,1476],{},[297,1472,1473,1475],{},[38,1474,702],{}," must form rectangles",": a named area can't be L-shaped. Each area must be a contiguous rectangle. The rows must have the same number of cells.",[286,1478,1479,62,1482,1485,1486,1489],{},[297,1480,1481],{},"Grid lines are 1-indexed",[38,1483,1484],{},"grid-column: 1 \u002F 3"," spans from line 1 to line 3 (2 tracks). Negative numbers count from the end: ",[38,1487,1488],{},"-1"," is the last line.",[286,1491,1492,1497,1498,1501],{},[297,1493,1494,1496],{},[38,1495,898],{}," in grid is between tracks, not around",": there's no padding-like gap at the edges. Use ",[38,1499,1500],{},"padding"," on the container for edge spacing.",[286,1503,1504,1507,1508,1511,1512,1515,1516,1518],{},[297,1505,1506],{},"Implicit tracks have default sizing",": items placed outside the defined tracks create implicit tracks with ",[38,1509,1510],{},"grid-auto-rows","\u002F",[38,1513,1514],{},"grid-auto-columns"," sizing (default ",[38,1517,107],{},").",[286,1520,1521,1526],{},[297,1522,1523,1525],{},[38,1524,994],{}," can reorder items visually",": later items fill earlier gaps, potentially placing a later item before an earlier one visually. Good for filling gaps, but can confuse reading order.",[286,1528,1529,1532],{},[297,1530,1531],{},"Subgrid browser support",": shipped in all major browsers in 2023. For older browsers, nested grids don't align with the parent's tracks — use explicit sizing or accept the misalignment.",[286,1534,1535,1541,1542,1544,1545,1548],{},[297,1536,1537,1538],{},"Grid and ",[38,1539,1540],{},"min-width: auto",": like flex items, grid items have ",[38,1543,1540],{}," by default and won't shrink below content. Set ",[38,1546,1547],{},"min-width: 0"," on items with long content.",[23,1550,1552],{"id":1551},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[14,1554,1555],{},"A developer makes a 2-column grid, but the first column (with long text) is wider than expected, and the second column is squeezed:",[28,1557,1558],{"language":30},[32,1559,1561],{"className":34,"code":1560,"language":30,"meta":36,"style":36},".grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }\n.col1 { \u002F* long text *\u002F }\n",[38,1562,1563,1592],{"__ignoreMap":36},[41,1564,1565,1568,1570,1572,1574,1576,1578,1580,1582,1584,1586,1588,1590],{"class":43,"line":44},[41,1566,1567],{"class":47},".grid",[41,1569,503],{"class":51},[41,1571,1043],{"class":58},[41,1573,62],{"class":51},[41,1575,65],{"class":58},[41,1577,1050],{"class":51},[41,1579,171],{"class":58},[41,1581,62],{"class":51},[41,1583,131],{"class":58},[41,1585,89],{"class":82},[41,1587,86],{"class":58},[41,1589,89],{"class":82},[41,1591,684],{"class":51},[41,1593,1594,1597,1599,1602],{"class":43,"line":55},[41,1595,1596],{"class":47},".col1",[41,1598,503],{"class":51},[41,1600,1601],{"class":95},"\u002F* long text *\u002F",[41,1603,1604],{"class":51}," }\n",[14,1606,1607],{},"What's wrong?",[1609,1610,1611,1615,1629,1635,1689,1705],"details",{},[1612,1613,1614],"summary",{},"Answer",[14,1616,1617,1619,1620,1622,1623,1625,1626,1628],{},[38,1618,1456],{}," has an implicit minimum of ",[38,1621,107],{}," (the content's minimum size). The first column's content (long text) has a large minimum width, so the column won't shrink below it — the ",[38,1624,1456],{}," distributes only the ",[18,1627,205],{}," space, which is little after the first column's content min is satisfied. The second column gets squeezed.",[14,1630,1631,1632,1634],{},"The fix — use ",[38,1633,1446],{}," to allow the columns to shrink below content size:",[32,1636,1638],{"className":34,"code":1637,"language":30,"meta":36,"style":36},".grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }\n",[38,1639,1640],{"__ignoreMap":36},[41,1641,1642,1644,1646,1648,1650,1652,1654,1656,1658,1660,1662,1665,1667,1669,1671,1674,1676,1678,1680,1682,1684,1686],{"class":43,"line":44},[41,1643,1567],{"class":47},[41,1645,503],{"class":51},[41,1647,1043],{"class":58},[41,1649,62],{"class":51},[41,1651,65],{"class":58},[41,1653,1050],{"class":51},[41,1655,171],{"class":58},[41,1657,62],{"class":51},[41,1659,348],{"class":58},[41,1661,340],{"class":51},[41,1663,1664],{"class":58},"0",[41,1666,345],{"class":51},[41,1668,131],{"class":58},[41,1670,89],{"class":82},[41,1672,1673],{"class":51},") ",[41,1675,348],{"class":58},[41,1677,340],{"class":51},[41,1679,1664],{"class":58},[41,1681,345],{"class":51},[41,1683,131],{"class":58},[41,1685,89],{"class":82},[41,1687,1688],{"class":51},"); }\n",[14,1690,1691,1692,1694,1695,1698,1699,1701,1702,1704],{},"::\nOr set ",[38,1693,1547],{}," on the items and add ",[38,1696,1697],{},"overflow-wrap: break-word"," for the text. ",[38,1700,1446],{}," tells the grid the column can shrink to 0 (below content), so the ",[38,1703,1456],{}," distributes space evenly.",[14,1706,1707,62,1710,1459,1712,1714,1715,1717],{},[297,1708,1709],{},"The lesson",[38,1711,1456],{},[38,1713,107],{}," (content size), so a column with long content won't shrink, squeezing others. Use ",[38,1716,1446],{}," for columns that should share space evenly regardless of content.",[23,1719,1720],{"id":1612},"Summary",[14,1722,1723,1724,345,1726,345,1728,345,1730,1511,1732,1734,1735,1737,1738,1740,1741,1743,1744,1746],{},"You can now build g